# System files
# Testing
# WhatsApp-Web bridge — Chromium session + cache. These churn every time
# account — sensitive session data and large binary files.
# code, and the auth payload is per-machine. Keep on disk so the bridge
# cookies, localStorage, IndexedDB and cache for each Amazon/Bigship
# product cards. Anything inside a sub-dir (claude_files/, dealer_*/,
# stay tracked since they were already committed and are referenced from
# stays logged in; just don't track them.
# the bridge runs (Chromium auto-updates its internal data dirs), aren't
# warranty_invoices/, etc.) is user-uploaded runtime data — never commit.
